<title>USA: Emco sells plastic division to syndicate.</title>
<headline>Emco sells plastic division to syndicate.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Emco Ltd said Wednesday it has sold its Waltec plastics division to a syndicate of investors led by HAIFinance Corp, a Washington-based holding company.</p>
<p>Emco said it will continue to be a shareholder of Waltec Plastics through a $1.55 million investment in preferred shares.</p>
<p>Terms were not disclosed. However, Emco said it expects to reduce its debt by about $10 million as a result of the sale.</p>
<p>Waltec Plastics manufactures custom-molded plastic parts.</p>
<p>Emco is a Canadian distributor and manufacturer of building materials.</p>
</text>
